    "title": "The New Neighbours",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Last month, a new family moved into the flat next to mine. There are four people: a father, a mother and two girls. They come from Poland. The father's name is Marek, and the mother's name is Ewa."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "On the first day, I said hello and gave them some cake. Ewa was very happy. She said, 'Thank you! You are very kind.' Her English is good, but Marek's English is not very good, so he is learning at an evening class."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The girls are called Zosia and Kasia. Zosia is nine and Kasia is twelve. They go to the school near our building. Zosia likes drawing, and Kasia likes music. She plays the piano every evening. I can hear it through the wall, and I like it."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Last Saturday they invited me for dinner. We ate soup and a special Polish dish with potatoes and meat. It was delicious! After dinner, Marek showed me photos of their old home. It is a small town near a big forest. I hope they are happy here."
      }
    ]
  },
